-- Zyrqon Nova 3.5 "Apex"
-- Standalone chess-analysis API.
--
-- Public interface:
--     local move, score = ZyrqonNova:GetBestMoveFromFEN(fen, seconds)
--
-- The engine keeps the same public API as the previous version, but uses:
--   * legal move generation with complete castling/en-passant handling
--   * deterministic dual 32-bit Zobrist hashing
--   * iterative deepening + aspiration windows
--   * transposition table with EXACT/LOWER/UPPER bounds
--   * principal-variation search
--   * killer + history + counter-move ordering
--   * null-move pruning with verification safeguards
--   * late-move reductions
--   * tactical quiescence including checks/promotions
--   * tapered middlegame/endgame evaluation
--   * pawn structure, mobility, king safety, rook files, bishop pair,
--     outposts, passed pawns and king activity
--   * repetition / immediate-reversal avoidance for repeated API calls
--   * cooperative time slicing for Roblox responsiveness
--
-- It is still a compact Lua engine, not a Stockfish-class 5000-Elo engine.
-- Strength is primarily limited by CPU time and the absence of Syzygy/NNUE.

